# What may go into a container build context, as an allowlist.
#
# Ignore everything first, then name the few directories the ingest image
# needs. An allowlist rather than a list of exclusions, because the things that
# must never reach a build context are exactly the things nobody remembers to
# exclude: hazard media under media/, private keys, the .git history, the
# app's node_modules, cdk.out.
#
# Check it before you build:
#
#   make image-context     prints every file the build would send
*

!flashmap/
!pipeline/
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Nothing generated, and no tests, even from the directories above. The tests
# are not part of either package, and flashmap/tests/fixtures/ holds video.
flashmap/**/__pycache__/
flashmap/tests/
flashmap/.hypothesis/
flashmap/build/
flashmap/dist/
flashmap/*.egg-info/
# An editable install of flashmap (the venv has one) writes its egg-info under
# src/, where the line above does not reach.
flashmap/**/*.egg-info/
flashmap/.pytest_cache/
pipeline/**/__pycache__/
pipeline/tests/
pipeline/infra/cdk.out/
# The CDK's lookup cache. A real deploy writes it next to cdk.json, and it holds
# an availability zone lookup keyed by the account id. The image pushed on
# Oct 9, 2026 carried one, because the deploy wrote it minutes before the build.
pipeline/infra/cdk.context.json
**/*.pyc
**/*.pem
**/.DS_Store

# Tool caches; never part of the image.
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
